title: The repository lock
tags: Daemon [[Key invariants]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: A daemon holds each loaded store under an exclusive flock; a second daemon's load is refused at once.

A repository's store is held under an exclusive lock — an `flock` on
`internal/kv/daemon.lock` — for the whole lifetime of the daemon's handle on it.
A second daemon instance therefore cannot load the same repository, which would
make the two drift: one daemon's watcher updating paths and versions while the
other commits a sync.

A load that finds the lock held is refused ''immediately'' with `409`, naming the
cause: another metafolder daemon is using the repository. Waiting would be
pointless — the lock belongs to a live daemon. A transient holder, such as a child
process that inherited the descriptor for an instant, is waited out for a second.

The lock is released by an unload, or by the process ending. For the tasks not to
keep it held past an unload, see [[Why background tasks hold a weak reference]].
